lemo-opuscar (MIT License) — https://github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Voice/Audio engine (motor 5) and the subtitle export of audiovisual-ia reuse
MIT-licensed code from the lemo-opuscar project ("core/" tree). Only the MIT code
is reused; lemo-opuscar's documentation (CC BY-NC 4.0), its demo films (CC BY 4.0),
the excluded demo narrations, the "Clawd" character and third-party marks/assets
are NOT reused.

Reused components (adapted behind audiovisual-ia's provider interfaces):

  - core/tts/tts.py       Kokoro offline TTS  -> app/providers/tts/kokoro.py
  - core/tts/tts_zh.py    edge-tts (online)   -> app/providers/tts/edge.py
  - core/tts/asr_check.py faster-whisper ASR  -> app/providers/asr/faster_whisper.py
  - core/render/srt.py    SRT export format   -> app/engines/voice/subtitles.py
  - core/render/mux.sh    FFmpeg loudnorm/mix -> app/engines/voice/mixer.py (-14 LUFS)

The kokoro.py and edge.py providers invoke the original lemo-opuscar scripts via
subprocess (located by AIV_LEMO_OPUSCAR_PATH), so the upstream MIT code runs
unmodified. The ASR, subtitle and mixer modules reimplement the same approach.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
JustCarlos30/skills-videos-cortos (MIT License)
https://github.com/JustCarlos30/skills-videos-cortos
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following modules of audiovisual-ia are ORIGINAL, independent reimplementations
(not literal copies) INSPIRED BY the MIT-licensed audio/voice workflow of
skills/voz-whisper/scripts/voz.py in JustCarlos30/skills-videos-cortos:

  - app/engines/voice/master.py     Voice cleanup + mastering chain to -14 LUFS
                                    (highpass / afftdn de-noise / de-esser / soft EQ /
                                    acompressor, then 2-pass loudnorm + alimiter).
  - app/engines/voice/trim.py       Silence trimming via ffmpeg silencedetect with
                                    speech-segment building and cumulative WordTiming
                                    re-mapping onto the trimmed timeline.
  - app/engines/voice/subtitles.py  Word-by-word subtitle cues, a palabras.json
                                    ([{text,startMs,endMs}]) export, and a corrections
                                    dictionary ({"mal":"bien"}) that redistributes the
                                    original token's time across replacement words.
  - app/engines/voice/recorded.py   Optional recorded-voice backend (upload -> master ->
                                    ASR -> subtitles), same Assets as the TTS path.

No source code from skills-videos-cortos is copied; only the techniques are adapted to
audiovisual-ia's own architecture (FFmpeg filter graphs and provider layer are our own).
The projects/<slug> layout, video.json and the Audacity .aup3 parser of voz.py are NOT
reused.

